- **src/pages/[[...slug]].tsx** (`Page`): Attachment point for Live Preview: this is where ContentstackContext.Provider wraps the entire page (line 39) and where getStaticProps fetches CMS data (line 74). Live Preview must intercept/update the content value passed to the provider when the CMS emits real-time edits. The 147 consumers via useContent will automatically re-render when the context value changes.
  - **Minimal fix:** Make the content passed to ContentstackContext.Provider reactive to live preview updates. In the Page component, add state for content initialized from props, subscribe to Contentstack's onEntryChange callback (from @contentstack/live-preview-utils), and on each callback merge the incoming live-preview entry into the existing content state (reusing the same shape: { page: [entry], header, footer, directories, ... }). Replace line 39's static `value={content}` with `value={liveContent}` where liveContent is the state updated by onEntryChange. Also initialize the live preview SDK (livePreviewInit) at app entry or in getStaticProps. The refineClientData util (already imported on line 16) should be reused to transform the live-preview entry the same way static entries are refined.

